Size: the content shell without Chromium's test support.

The content shell links the test support of content/, Views, Aura and the
device service for the browser tests that run inside it, and with it a
benchmark library, test services, the on-device model service, TFLite and
the SPIR-V tools. A GN argument, content_shell_test_support, leaves it out.
The services only tests use (the test, echo and Rust test services, the
sandbox status helper, the internals object) are then not built, under
CONTENT_SHELL_TEST_SUPPORT, which content_shell_lib exports so that every
user of its headers sees the same classes.

What the shell needs of the test support it compiles itself: a background
sync controller and an accept-language delegate, which content requires,
the registry behind navigator.registerProtocolHandler(), and the Views
delegate its windows are made with. The feature list comes
from the command line, in place of SetupFieldTrials(), which also applies
Chromium's testing configuration of field trials: the engine runs with
Chromium's default features, as a browser does.

Off in profiles/slim.gn. Upstream's default is unchanged.

